From: xcentaurix
Subject: [PATCH] WPE: join and register with Nexus before any EGL call, on Nexus-based Broadcom boxes

On a Nexus-based Broadcom box (GigaBlue gbquad4kpro confirmed 2026-09-23; likely other Nexus-middleware boxes too, e.g. VU+ Ultimo 4K - same "Memory
interface not registered" signature, not yet retested with this exact fix), eglInitialize() aborts:

  ASSERT at libs/platform/bcg_abstract/gmem_abstract.c:132:gmem_init
  Memory interface not registered

Root-caused with a standalone diagnostic tool (tools/vuplus-probe in the hbbtv2 repo; see vu_egl_probe.c and project memory
project_hbbtv2_wpe_orb_plan.md for the full trace through dynsym_dump symbol listings and Broadcom's own header dump) rather than guessed at:

 - NxClient_Join() (libnxclient.so) - the general Nexus client/server IPC join - is necessary but, confirmed by testing, NOT sufficient alone: it
   succeeds (returns 0) but eglInitialize() still asserts identically afterward.
 - NXPL_RegisterNexusDisplayPlatform() (libnxpl.so) is the missing piece. Broadcom's own header (hbbtv2/headers/gb-nexus-headers/default_nexus.h,
   "Default Nexus platform API for EGL driver") declares it and documents it as: "Register a display for exclusive use ... It will register its own
   memory, h/w and display APIs suitable for basic exclusive mode rendering on a Nexus display." - matching the assertion text exactly.
 - In multi-process client mode (the normal case here, not SINGLE_PROCESS) NEXUS_DISPLAYHANDLE is just void*, not a real handle from the
   single-process-only NEXUS_Display_Open() - passing NULL works and was verified end-to-end: eglInitialize() succeeds (EGL 1.5) immediately after
   this call, in an isolated test tool, with the live TV picture confirmed unaffected during the test.

Fix: PlatformDisplayDefault::create() - the one place this fork's EGL bring-up goes through for every board, Nexus-based or not - now does the
join+register sequence once per process before its existing eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY) call, and unregisters in the destructor. Pure runtime
detection via dlopen/dlsym: no Nexus SDK headers and no link-time dependency on libnxclient.so/libnxpl.so, so this is a true no-op - confirmed via a
regression test on the DM900 that produces zero related log output - on any platform without them (this fork's other target, the DM900's
libvc5dream stack, has no Nexus/NxClient/NXPL at all).

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/PlatformDisplayDefault.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/PlatformDisplayDefault.cpp
index 72b3bf9d..c50da7ea 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/PlatformDisplayDefault.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/PlatformDisplayDefault.cpp
@@ -31,10 +31,73 @@
 #include "GLContext.h"
 #include <epoxy/egl.h>

+#if PLATFORM(WPE)
+#include <cstring>
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#endif
+
 namespace WebCore {

+#if PLATFORM(WPE)
+// Nexus-based Broadcom boxes (GigaBlue gbquad4kpro confirmed 2026-09-23; likely other Nexus-middleware boxes too, e.g. VU+
+// Ultimo 4K - same "Memory interface not registered" signature, not yet retested with this exact fix) need two calls before
+// any EGL call can succeed: NxClient_Join() (join the Nexus client/server IPC bus - necessary but, confirmed by testing, NOT
+// sufficient alone) and NXPL_RegisterNexusDisplayPlatform() (libnxpl.so; its own doc comment says it "registers its own
+// memory, h/w and display APIs" for the display - the literal, exact cause of "Memory interface not registered" at
+// gmem_abstract.c:132 otherwise). Passing NULL for the display argument works: in multi-process client mode
+// NEXUS_DISPLAYHANDLE is just void* (not a real handle from the single-process-only NEXUS_Display_Open), and this box's
+// vendor driver resolves it against the already-joined default display.
+//
+// Pure runtime detection via dlopen/dlsym, no Nexus SDK headers and no link-time dependency on libnxclient.so/libnxpl.so, so
+// this safely no-ops on every platform that doesn't have them (e.g. the DM900's libvc5dream stack, which has no
+// Nexus/NxClient/NXPL at all). Root-caused and verified end-to-end (including that the live picture is unaffected) via
+// tools/vuplus-probe in the hbbtv2 repo before being written here - see that tool's vu_egl_probe.c for the exact sequence
+// this mirrors, and project memory (project_hbbtv2_wpe_orb_plan.md) for the full trace through Broadcom's own header dump
+// that found NXPL_RegisterNexusDisplayPlatform in the first place.
+static void* s_nxplPlatformHandle;
+static void (*s_nxplUnregisterDisplayPlatform)(void*);
+
+static void ensureNexusPlatformJoined()
+{
+    static bool attempted = false;
+    if (attempted)
+        return;
+    attempted = true;
+
+    if (void* nxclient = dlopen("libnxclient.so", RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL)) {
+        auto getDefaultJoinSettings = reinterpret_cast<void (*)(void*)>(dlsym(nxclient, "NxClient_GetDefaultJoinSettings"));
+        auto join = reinterpret_cast<int (*)(const void*)>(dlsym(nxclient, "NxClient_Join"));
+        if (getDefaultJoinSettings && join) {
+            // The real NxClient_JoinSettings layout needs the proprietary Nexus SDK headers, not available at build time here.
+            // Safe without them: GetDefaultJoinSettings() only WRITES into this buffer and Join() only reads back what was
+            // just written, so any buffer at least as large as the real struct works (known Broadcom SDKs: well under 200
+            // bytes; 1024 is generous headroom).
+            unsigned char joinSettings[1024];
+            memset(joinSettings, 0, sizeof(joinSettings));
+            getDefaultJoinSettings(joinSettings);
+            int rc = join(joinSettings);
+            WTFLogAlways("NxClient_Join() returned %d (0 = NEXUS_SUCCESS)", rc);
+        }
+    }
+
+    if (void* nxpl = dlopen("libnxpl.so", RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL)) {
+        auto registerDisplayPlatform = reinterpret_cast<void (*)(void**, void*)>(dlsym(nxpl, "NXPL_RegisterNexusDisplayPlatform"));
+        s_nxplUnregisterDisplayPlatform = reinterpret_cast<void (*)(void*)>(dlsym(nxpl, "NXPL_UnregisterNexusDisplayPlatform"));
+        if (registerDisplayPlatform && s_nxplUnregisterDisplayPlatform) {
+            registerDisplayPlatform(&s_nxplPlatformHandle, nullptr);
+            WTFLogAlways("NXPL_RegisterNexusDisplayPlatform() -> handle=%p", s_nxplPlatformHandle);
+        } else
+            s_nxplUnregisterDisplayPlatform = nullptr;
+    }
+}
+#endif // PLATFORM(WPE)
+
 std::unique_ptr<PlatformDisplayDefault> PlatformDisplayDefault::create()
 {
+#if PLATFORM(WPE)
+    ensureNexusPlatformJoined();
+#endif
+
     auto glDisplay = GLDisplay::create(eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY));
     if (!glDisplay) {
         WTFLogAlways("Could not create default EGL display: %s. Aborting...", GLContext::lastErrorString());
@@ -53,7 +116,15 @@ PlatformDisplayDefault::PlatformDisplayDefault(Ref<GLDisplay>&& glDisplay)
 #endif
 }

-PlatformDisplayDefault::~PlatformDisplayDefault() = default;
+PlatformDisplayDefault::~PlatformDisplayDefault()
+{
+#if PLATFORM(WPE)
+    if (s_nxplUnregisterDisplayPlatform && s_nxplPlatformHandle) {
+        s_nxplUnregisterDisplayPlatform(s_nxplPlatformHandle);
+        s_nxplPlatformHandle = nullptr;
+    }
+#endif
+}

 } // namespace WebCore

